      "html": "<big><span dir=\"rtl\">אֱמֹרִי</span></big>  <strong>s.pr.m. coletivo</strong> (construído como plural <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.9\">Dt 3:9</a> + 5 ocorrências) <strong>amorreus (</strong>talvez = <em>habitantes das montanhas</em>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:29\" href=\"/Numbers.13.29\">Nu 13:29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.7\">Dt 1:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.19\">19 f.</a> etc. e Di <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:16\" href=\"/Genesis.10.16\">Gn 10:16</a> e outros.<strong>)</strong> — sempre com artigo, exceto <a data-ref=\"Numbers 21:29\" href=\"/Numbers.21.29\">Nu 21:29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:45\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.45\">Ez 16:45</a>. O significado <em>habitantes das montanhas</em> é muito duvidoso; sobre <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> = egípcio <em>ʾA-ma-ra</em> ver WMM<sup>As. u. Eur. 229 ss.</sup>, = das cartas de Tel el-Amarna e assírio <em>Amurru</em>, ver Wkl<sup>TelAm. 36</sup> Jastr<sup>EB Canaan, § 10</sup> Say<sup>HastDB Amorites</sup> e outros; cf. também GFM; <a data-ref=\"Judges 4\" href=\"/Judges.4\">Ju 4</a>,<a data-ref=\"Judges 5\" href=\"/Judges.5\">5</a> Dr <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.7\">Dt 1:7</a> Gray <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:29\" href=\"/Numbers.13.29\">Nu 13:29</a>.<br><strong>1.</strong>  chamado filho de Canaã <a data-ref=\"Genesis 10:16\" href=\"/Genesis.10.16\">Gn 10:16</a> (J) <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 1:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.1.14\">1 Ch 1:14</a> =<br><strong>2.</strong>  um dos principais povos desalojados pelos hebreus; (<em>a</em>) habitando a leste do Jordão <a data-ref=\"Numbers 21:13\" href=\"/Numbers.21.13\">Nu 21:13</a>,<sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 21:25\" href=\"/Numbers.21.25\">25</a> + 9 ocorrências em Números + <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:8\" href=\"/Joshua.24.8\">Jos 24:8</a> (todas E), cf. <a data-ref=\"Joshua 2:10\" href=\"/Joshua.2.10\">Jos 2:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 9:10\" href=\"/Joshua.9.10\">9:10</a> (JE) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.4\">Dt 1:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:2\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.2\">3:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.9\">9</a> + 7 ocorrências em D; também <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:8\" href=\"/Judges.10.8\">Ju 10:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:11\" href=\"/Judges.10.11\">11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:19\" href=\"/Judges.11.19\">11:19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:21\" href=\"/Judges.11.21\">21</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:22\" href=\"/Judges.11.22\">22</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:23\" href=\"/Judges.11.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 4:19\" href=\"/I_Kings.4.19\">1 K 4:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 135:11\" href=\"/Psalms.135.11\">ψ 135:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 136:19\" href=\"/Psalms.136.19\">136:19</a> (Seom, rei deles, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 21:21\" href=\"/Numbers.21.21\">Nu 21:21</a> +; Seom e Ogue <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 3:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.3.8\">Dt 3:8</a> +); (<em>b</em>) habitando a oeste do Jordão <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:5\" href=\"/Joshua.10.5\">Jos 10:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:6\" href=\"/Joshua.10.6\">6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:12\" href=\"/Joshua.24.12\">24:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:15\" href=\"/Joshua.24.15\">15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:18\" href=\"/Joshua.24.18\">18</a> (todas E), cf. <a data-ref=\"Joshua 7:7\" href=\"/Joshua.7.7\">7:7</a> (JE); <a data-ref=\"Joshua 5:1\" href=\"/Joshua.5.1\">5:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:12\" href=\"/Joshua.10.12\">10:12</a> (ambas D; cf. também <a data-ref=\"Joshua 13:4\" href=\"/Joshua.13.4\">13:4</a>, cuja supressão é proposta por Di) <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:34\" href=\"/Judges.1.34\">Ju 1:34</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:35\" href=\"/Judges.1.35\">35</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:36\" href=\"/Judges.1.36\">36</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:10\" href=\"/Judges.6.10\">6:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:26\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.26\">1 K 21:26</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 21:11\" href=\"/II_Kings.21.11\">2 K 21:11</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 7:14\" href=\"/I_Samuel.7.14\">1 S 7:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 21:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.21.2\">2 S 21:2</a>; (<em>c</em>) habitando ao sul <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.7\">Dt 1:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:27\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.27\">27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:44\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.44\">44</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:7\" href=\"/Genesis.14.7\">Gn 14:7</a> (a oeste do mar Morto); (<em>d</em>) em sentido geral = antigos habitantes de Canaã <a data-ref=\"Genesis 15:16\" href=\"/Genesis.15.16\">Gn 15:16</a> (J ou R) <a data-ref=\"Genesis 48:22\" href=\"/Genesis.48.22\">48:22</a> (E) <a data-ref=\"Amos 2:9\" href=\"/Amos.2.9\">Am 2:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Amos 2:10\" href=\"/Amos.2.10\">10</a>; (<em>e</em>) mencionado em listas de povos cananeus destinados a ser desalojados por Israel <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:8\" href=\"/Exodus.3.8\">Ex 3:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 3:17\" href=\"/Exodus.3.17\">17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 13:5\" href=\"/Exodus.13.5\">13:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 33:2\" href=\"/Exodus.33.2\">33:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 34:11\" href=\"/Exodus.34.11\">34:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 3:10\" href=\"/Joshua.3.10\">Jos 3:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 9:1\" href=\"/Joshua.9.1\">9:1</a> (todas J); <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 7:1\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.7.1\">Dt 7:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 20:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.20.17\">20:17</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:3\" href=\"/Joshua.11.3\">Jos 11:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 12:8\" href=\"/Joshua.12.8\">12:8</a> (todas D); <a data-ref=\"Exodus 23:23\" href=\"/Exodus.23.23\">Ex 23:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:29\" href=\"/Numbers.13.29\">Nu 13:29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:11\" href=\"/Joshua.24.11\">Jos 24:11</a> (todas E); <a data-ref=\"Judges 3:5\" href=\"/Judges.3.5\">Ju 3:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 9:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.9.20\">1 K 9:20</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 8:7\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.8.7\">2 Ch 8:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:1\" href=\"/Ezra.9.1\">Ezr 9:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 9:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.9.8\">Ne 9:8</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:3\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.3\">Ez 16:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:45\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.45\">45</a>; (sobre essas listas, cf. Bu<sup>Urgesch 344 ss.</sup> e We<sup>JBTh xxi. 602</sup>.)<br><strong>3.</strong>  <strong>adj. gentílico</strong> singular <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:13\" href=\"/Genesis.14.13\">Gn 14:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:24\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.24\">Dt 2:24</a>.",
